BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aamas-2027-deadline-abstract@scientific-conference-calendar
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART:20261002T115900Z
DTEND:20261002T125900Z
SUMMARY:[Machine Learning][Reinforcement Learning] AAMAS 2027 - Main-track 
 abstract registration deadline
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: International Conference on Autonomous Agents
  and Multiagent Systems\nWebsite: https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/dcs/aamas
 2027/\nSource URL: https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/dcs/aamas2027/calls/call
 -for-main-track/\nLocation: Hanoi\, Vietnam\nTopics: Machine Learning\, R
 einforcement Learning\, Autonomous Agents & Multiagent Systems\, Human-AI
  Interaction & Deployment\nSize: XL\nSubmission type: Paper-based / Blue 
 Sky Ideas short papers\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10
 -07\nNotes: Annual flagship meeting in Hanoi. New main-track submissions 
 are closed because the Oct 1 abstract gate has passed\, even before the O
 ct 8 paper cutoff. The separate four-page Blue Sky Ideas track remains a 
 forthcoming opportunity\; author registration is announced for Oct 20 but
  no exact opening hour is given. Its Nov 5 gate only controls its Nov 12 
 short papers. AAAI fast-track and already published JAAMAS presentations 
 are not general new-paper routes. Size XL is an editorial estimate. Histo
 rical acceptance covers main full papers only\, not Blue Sky Ideas or the
  newly introduced 2027 Findings track.\nScope: Autonomous agents and mult
 i-agent systems: learning and adaptation\, coordination\, game theory\, p
 lanning\, reasoning\, agent engineering\, and agent-based simulation. Als
 o covers human-agent interaction\, robot teams\, norms and governance\, a
 nd generative agents. The contribution should concern agents or their int
 eraction\; generic language-model or learning results are not automatical
 ly in scope.\nAdditional topics: Deep Representation Learning\, Probabili
 stic\, Causal & Uncertainty ML\, Control & Robotics\, Complex Systems & N
 etwork Science\, Ethics & Governance\, Explainability & Interpretability\
 nScope sources (2027): https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/dcs/aamas2027/calls/
 call-for-main-track/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/dcs/aamas2027/calls/call-for-main-track/
END:VEVENT
